========================================
 position: relative
========================================

DEFINITION:

position: relative; positions an element relative to its
original (normal flow) position while still keeping it
inside the normal document flow.


----------------------------------------
HOW POSITION: RELATIVE WORKS
----------------------------------------

1) The browser first places the element normally.
2) Then it shifts the element visually using offset properties.
3) The original space of the element is still reserved.


----------------------------------------
SYNTAX
----------------------------------------

selector {
    position: relative;
}


----------------------------------------
KEY CHARACTERISTICS
----------------------------------------

- Remains in normal document flow
- Original space is preserved
- Can be moved using:
  top
  left
  right
  bottom
- z-index works
- Can overlap other elements
- Does NOT remove element from layout
- Creates a positioning reference for absolute children


----------------------------------------
VERY IMPORTANT RULES
----------------------------------------

1) If no offset values are given,
   it behaves exactly like position: static;

2) Moving the element does NOT affect
   the position of other elements.

3) The empty space of its original position
   still remains in the layout.

4) z-index works only on positioned elements
   (position must NOT be static).

5) It creates a positioning context for
   child elements with position: absolute.


----------------------------------------
OFFSET DIRECTION RULE
----------------------------------------

top: 20px;     -> moves element DOWN
bottom: 20px;  -> moves element UP
left: 20px;    -> moves element RIGHT
right: 20px;   -> moves element LEFT


----------------------------------------
EXAMPLE
----------------------------------------

HTML:

<div class="box">Relative Box</div>


CSS:

.box {
    width: 150px;
    height: 150px;
    background-color: lightgreen;
    position: relative;
    top: 20px;
    left: 30px;
}


----------------------------------------
OUTPUT BEHAVIOR
----------------------------------------

- Box moves 20px down
- Box moves 30px right
- Original space remains
- Other elements are not affected
- Layout structure does not change


----------------------------------------
REAL-WORLD USAGE
----------------------------------------

- Small UI adjustments
- Creating parent reference for absolute elements
- Using z-index for layering
- Adjusting icons, badges, labels
- Overlapping elements intentionally


----------------------------------------
INTERVIEW ANSWER
----------------------------------------

Relative positioning moves an element relative to its
original position while keeping it in normal document flow.
Offset properties and z-index work, and the original space
remains reserved.


----------------------------------------
SUMMARY
----------------------------------------

- Default behavior + manual shifting
- Remains in normal flow
- Space is preserved
- Offset properties work
- z-index works
- Creates positioning context
- Does not disturb surrounding layout
